\" font-weight=\"800\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">due_date</text><text x=\"695\" y=\"328\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"820\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#db9566\">null</text><text x=\"841\" y=\"328\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"680\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">string | null</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"407\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"700\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">The validator checks keys and types; another check must confirm the source values.</text></svg></div><p class=\"sout-note\">Illustrative invoice examples. Schema adherence and factual truth require separate checks.</p></section>",
  "questions": [
    {
      "stem": "What is Structured Output in Prompt Engineering, and why is a predictable data structure more useful to software than an unrestricted natural-language response?",
      "tag": "Beginner · Data contracts",
      "options": [
        "Structured Output asks a model to respond in readable paragraphs and adds field names afterward when needed. Applications can infer types and missing values from prose without a defined response contract.",
        "Structured Output asks a model to return data in an agreed shape with defined fields and types, such as JSON. Software can validate and process it more reliably than free-form prose.",
        "Structured Output means the model always calls a function rather than answering the user. A function call is required even when the application only needs a JSON object for display.",
        "Structured Output formats a model response as a text table with regular headings. Those headings are sufficient to guarantee each value has the expected data type and meaning."
      ],
      "answer": "b",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Structured Output means asking a model to return information using a predictable structure, such as a JSON object with known field names and types. This lets an application parse and validate results instead of guessing where facts appear in prose. For an invoice assistant, software can read `order_id` and `total` directly. A required structure makes automation easier, but field values still need factual checks.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"sout-figure\"><span class=\"sout-kicker\">QUESTION 01 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"sout-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 430\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"so-rev1t so-rev1d\"><title id=\"so-rev1t\">Free-form prose cannot guarantee a field contract</title><desc id=\"so-rev1d\">A single invoice sentence and two semantic key markers are contrasted with JSON text containing explicit order_id string and numeric total.</desc><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1000\" height=\"430\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"40\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">01 · STRUCTURED OUTPUT</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"79\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"24\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">Free-form prose cannot guarantee a field contract</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"120\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"840\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">FREE-FORM SENTENCE VS A FIELD-LEVEL CONTRACT</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"182\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"750\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">“Order A-240 costs $18.50.”</text><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"199\" x2=\"490\" y2=\"199\" stroke=\"#448eaf\" stroke-width=\"4\" /><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"284\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#448eaf\"/><text x=\"122\" y=\"290\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"820\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#448eaf\">order_id</text><circle cx=\"321\" cy=\"284\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#299980\"/><text x=\"343\" y=\"290\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"820\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">total</text><line x1=\"512\" y1=\"217\" x2=\"566\" y2=\"217\" stroke=\"#7a80af\" stroke-width=\"3\" /><path d=\"M557 209 L566 217 L557 225\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7a80af\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"598\" y=\"151\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#7a80af\">JSON OBJECT</text><text x=\"590\" y=\"204\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"780\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">{ &quot;order_id&quot;: &quot;A-240&quot;,</text><text x=\"613\" y=\"246\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"780\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">&quot;total&quot;: 18.50 }</text><line x1=\"592\" y1=\"273\" x2=\"925\" y2=\"273\" stroke=\"#7a80af\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 6\"/><text x=\"597\" y=\"303\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#448eaf\">keys</text><text x=\"738\" y=\"303\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">types</text><text x=\"844\" y=\"303\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#db9566\">values</text><text x=\"57\" y=\"405\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"680\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">A parser can address known fields rather than search unrestricted prose for values.</text></svg></div><p class=\"sout-note\">JSON, function arguments and other structured formats serve related but distinct purposes.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "Why is valid JSON different from schema-conforming Structured Output, and how do required keys, field types and additional-property rules affect correctness?",
      "tag": "Beginner · JSON versus schema",
      "options": [
        "JSON parsing checks both syntax and business meaning, so a parsed object automatically has the intended required keys and correct numeric values. Separate schema validation adds little once parsing succeeds.",
        "Schema conformance only checks whether output can be decoded as JSON; type differences or unexpected keys do not matter. A response with extra fields is still guaranteed usable by every consumer.",
        "JSON mode and strict schema-based output constrain identical things, because both require exact field sets and data types. Either mode therefore prevents string values from appearing in numeric fields.",
        "JSON syntax ensures the text is parseable, while a schema can demand specific keys, types and permitted properties. Schema-conforming data can still contain factually incorrect values."
      ],
      "answer": "d",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> JSON syntax tells us whether text represents legal JSON. Schema checks go further: a field such as `total` may need to be numeric, `order_id` required, and unknown keys disallowed. A response containing `\"total\":\"18.50\"` is valid JSON but not a valid numeric field under that schema. An invoice app must check structure and then verify numbers against the original document. Even a schema-valid value may be wrong.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"sout-figure\"><span class=\"sout-kicker\">QUESTION 02 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"sout-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 430\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"so-rev2t so-rev2d\"><title id=\"so-rev2t\">A parseable object can fail three schema rules</title><desc id=\"so-rev2d\">A valid JSON object is inspected with four concrete test marks: syntax passes, but required order_id is missing, total is a string, and an unexpected extra key appears.</desc><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1000\" height=\"430\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"40\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">02 · STRUCTURED OUTPUT</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"79\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"24\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">A parseable object can fail three schema rules</text><text x=\"55\" y=\"118\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">PARSE SUCCESS DOES NOT IMPLY SCHEMA SUCCESS</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"161\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"760\" font-size=\"21\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">{ &quot;total&quot;: &quot;18.50&quot;, &quot;extra&quot;: &quot;note&quot; }</text><line x1=\"57\" y1=\"182\" x2=\"915\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"2\" /><circle cx=\"94\" cy=\"251\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#299980\"/><path d=\"M85 250 L93 258 L105 241\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#299980\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"68\" y=\"296\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">JSON syntax</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"323\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"700\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">well-formed object</text><circle cx=\"327\" cy=\"251\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#db9566\"/><path d=\"M319 242 L335 258 M335 242 L319 258\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#db9566\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"301\" y=\"296\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">required order_id</text><text x=\"301\" y=\"323\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"700\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">missing key</text><circle cx=\"560\" cy=\"251\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#db9566\"/><path d=\"M552 242 L568 258 M568 242 L552 258\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#db9566\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"534\" y=\"296\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">total is number</text><text x=\"534\" y=\"323\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"700\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">string, not number</text><circle cx=\"793\" cy=\"251\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#db9566\"/><path d=\"M785 242 L801 258 M801 242 L785 258\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#db9566\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"767\" y=\"296\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">no extra keys</text><text x=\"767\" y=\"323\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"700\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">unexpected extra</text><text x=\"55\" y=\"389\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"820\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#db9566\">✓ JSON parses     × Object violates the intended contract</text><text x=\"55\" y=\"416\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"660\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">Strict schema generation aims at both required keys and supported field types.</text></svg></div><p class=\"sout-note\">JSON mode and strict schema adherence are not equivalent guarantees.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "How can Structured Output describe required fields, nullable values and restricted keys when some information is genuinely missing from the input?",
      "tag": "Beginner · Required and nullable",
      "options": [
        "Define explicit field types, mark necessary keys as required and permit null where a value is unknown. In supported strict schemas, disallow extra properties to keep outputs predictable.",
        "Define every potentially missing field as a free-form string and ask the model to guess when input data is absent. This keeps the JSON keys consistent without needing null values.",
        "Remove required fields whenever the source omits them, and let the model create additional replacement keys. Changing the object shape per request is the simplest way to guarantee compatibility.",
        "Declare all object fields optional while keeping strict schema mode enabled, because optionality is supported identically across every JSON Schema implementation and every constrained-output provider."
      ],
      "answer": "a",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> A structured contract can require fields while allowing null for information the source does not contain. For example, `due_date` may have the type string or null and still be required as a key. In some providers' strict structured-output modes, all object keys must be marked required and extra properties disabled. For an invoice with no due date, returning JSON null is more truthful than inventing tomorrow's date. Always check the particular provider's supported schema subset.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"sout-figure\"><span class=\"sout-kicker\">QUESTION 03 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"sout-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 430\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"so-rev3t so-rev3d\"><title id=\"so-rev3t\">Required keys can legally contain null values</title><desc id=\"so-rev3d\">A three-row truth table compares a present string date, a present null date, and an absent required key. The first two pass a required nullable contract; the last fails.</desc><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1000\" height=\"430\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"40\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">03 · STRUCTURED OUTPUT</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"79\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"24\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">Required keys can legally contain null values</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"118\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">PRESENCE AND NULLABILITY ARE INDEPENDENT RULES</text><text x=\"57\" y=\"157\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"780\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">DUE DATE</text><text x=\"71\" y=\"200\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"780\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">&quot;due_date&quot;: &quot;2026-11-15&quot;</text><text x=\"567\" y=\"200\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"770\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">present</text><text x=\"740\" y=\"200\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"770\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">string</text><path d=\"M924 192 L932 200 L944 183\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#299980\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"57\" y1=\"224\" x2=\"943\" y2=\"224\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1\" /><text x=\"71\" y=\"268\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"780\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">&quot;due_date&quot;: null</text><text x=\"567\" y=\"268\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"770\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">present</text><text x=\"740\" y=\"268\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"770\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">null</text><path d=\"M924 260 L932 268 L944 251\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#299980\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"57\" y1=\"292\" x2=\"943\" y2=\"292\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1\" /><text x=\"71\" y=\"336\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"780\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#db9566\">(due_date key absent)</text><text x=\"567\" y=\"336\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"770\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#db9566\">missing</text><text x=\"740\" y=\"336\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"770\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#db9566\">undefined</text><path d=\"M925 320 L941 336 M941 320 L925 336\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#db9566\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"57\" y1=\"360\" x2=\"943\" y2=\"360\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1\" /><text x=\"560\" y=\"154\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"800\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">REQUIRED?</text><text x=\"735\" y=\"154\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"800\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">VALUE TYPE</text><text x=\"57\" y=\"411\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"690\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">If the field is required but not known, null avoids inventing a date.</text></svg></div><p class=\"sout-note\">Required nullable fields are useful when a downstream application expects a stable shape.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "Why must a Structured Output workflow verify extracted facts against the source, even when a model produces valid JSON that follows the declared schema?",
      "tag": "Medium · Extracted truth",
      "options": [
        "Once all keys and types pass schema validation, extracted facts are guaranteed to match the document. Any factual mismatch must instead be caused by the downstream system after parsing.",
        "Factual verification is only needed when an output schema has no numeric fields. Numeric values constrained by a JSON Schema are necessarily copied accurately from the source document.",
        "Schema validation checks a response's shape, not whether reported values are true. Compare important fields with the source and represent unavailable values as null instead of fabricating them.",
        "Structured output is safest when the model fills unspecified fields with plausible defaults. A complete-looking record should be preferred over nulls because missing values can break applications."
      ],
      "answer": "c",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Schema adherence controls data shape, but a model may still misread or invent facts. An object might have the correct keys and numeric types while reporting an invoice total of $81.50 instead of the source's $18.50. Validate important fields against source evidence and use null when details are missing. In a shipping-label extractor, this means checking tracking numbers, amounts and addresses rather than accepting every well-formed response. Shape validation and factual verification are separate responsibilities.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"sout-figure\"><span class=\"sout-kicker\">QUESTION 04 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"sout-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 430\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"so-rev4t so-rev4d\"><title id=\"so-rev4t\">A schema-valid numeric value can be $63 wrong</title><desc id=\"so-rev4d\">A true-to-scale number line from zero to one hundred marks invoice source total 18.50 and wrong extracted total 81.50. The gap equals 63.</desc><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1000\" height=\"430\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"40\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">04 · STRUCTURED OUTPUT</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"79\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"24\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">A schema-valid numeric value can be $63 wrong</text><text x=\"55\" y=\"120\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">SCHEMA-VALID WRONG NUMBERS NEED A SOURCE CHECK</text><line x1=\"101\" y1=\"336\" x2=\"873\" y2=\"336\" stroke=\"#819fae\" stroke-width=\"2\" /><line x1=\"101\" y1=\"159\" x2=\"101\" y2=\"336\" stroke=\"#819fae\" stroke-width=\"2\" /><line x1=\"101\" y1=\"330\" x2=\"101\" y2=\"345\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" /><text x=\"101\" y=\"371\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"690\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#668290\">0</text><line x1=\"255.4\" y1=\"330\" x2=\"255.4\" y2=\"345\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" /><text x=\"255.4\" y=\"371\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"690\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#668290\">20</text><line x1=\"409.8\" y1=\"330\" x2=\"409.8\" y2=\"345\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" /><text x=\"409.8\" y=\"371\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"690\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#668290\">40</text><line x1=\"564.2\" y1=\"330\" x2=\"564.2\" y2=\"345\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" /><text x=\"564.2\" y=\"371\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"690\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#668290\">60</text><line x1=\"718.6\" y1=\"330\" x2=\"718.6\" y2=\"345\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" /><text x=\"718.6\" y=\"371\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"690\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#668290\">80</text><line x1=\"873\" y1=\"330\" x2=\"873\" y2=\"345\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" /><text x=\"873\" y=\"371\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"690\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#668290\">100</text><circle cx=\"243.82\" cy=\"227\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#299980\"/><circle cx=\"730.18\" cy=\"227\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#db9566\"/><line x1=\"243.82\" y1=\"227\" x2=\"730.18\" y2=\"227\" stroke=\"#db9566\" stroke-width=\"5\" /><line x1=\"243.82\" y1=\"241\" x2=\"243.82\" y2=\"327\" stroke=\"#299980\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/><line x1=\"730.18\" y1=\"241\" x2=\"730.18\" y2=\"327\" stroke=\"#db9566\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/><text x=\"243.82\" y=\"196\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#299980\">$18.50</text><text x=\"730.18\" y=\"196\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#db9566\">$81.50</text><text x=\"487\" y=\"209\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"840\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#db9566\">Δ $63.00</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"415\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"675\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">Both amounts are valid numeric JSON values; only $18.50 matches the invoice.</text></svg></div><p class=\"sout-note\">Supported structured-generation methods improve format reliability, not truthfulness.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "How can a short Python program validate a Structured Output JSON example using required keys, exact data types, missing-value handling and source comparison?",
      "tag": "Medium · Python validation",
      "options": [
        "Parse stored JSON and check that keys are present, but treat numeric strings as valid numbers to preserve flexibility. If parsing succeeds, source totals do not need an independent comparison.",
        "Parse the JSON, check the exact keys and field types, accept a genuine missing date as null, and compare values against the source. Reject a numeric amount returned as a string.",
        "Ask a language model to generate a replacement JSON response whenever one field is mistyped, then count the repaired object as a successful first attempt. This measures schema reliability directly.",
        "Validate an illustrative example by checking that it contains a recognizable order identifier, then infer the remaining fields. Source consistency and extra keys can be handled after the record is stored."
      ],
      "answer": "b",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Python's `json` module can decode a stored output, after which ordinary checks enforce required keys and types. The example validates invoice A-240, total 18.50, and a null due date because none was supplied. It rejects a quoted numeric amount and verifies that the returned values match the source object. This tests a local validator rather than a language model. Production applications may use JSON Schema libraries for larger contracts and must still handle invalid or missing model responses.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"sout-figure\"><span class=\"sout-kicker\">QUESTION 05 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"sout-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 430\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"so-rev5t so-rev5d\"><title id=\"so-rev5t\">A local validator catches a quoted numeric amount</title><desc id=\"so-rev5d\">A four-row typed-field audit shows order_id, numeric total and null due_date passing, but a quoted total string failing. All values are illustrative local checks.</desc><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1000\" height=\"430\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"40\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">05 · STRUCTURED OUTPUT</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"79\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"24\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">A local validator catches a quoted numeric amount</text><text x=\"55\" y=\"120\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">LOCAL PYTHON CHECKS EXACT TYPES AND SOURCE MATCH</text><rect x=\"56\" y=\"161\" width=\"11\" height=\"40\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#299980\"/><text x=\"82\" y=\"187\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">order_id</text><text x=\"288\" y=\"187\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"770\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">&quot;A-240&quot;</text><text x=\"588\" y=\"187\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"730\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">string</text><path d=\"M854 178 L862 186 L874 169\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#299980\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"58\" y1=\"208\" x2=\"923\" y2=\"208\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1\" /><rect x=\"56\" y=\"215\" width=\"11\" height=\"40\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#299980\"/><text x=\"82\" y=\"241\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">total</text><text x=\"288\" y=\"241\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"770\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">18.50</text><text x=\"588\" y=\"241\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"730\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">number</text><path d=\"M854 232 L862 240 L874 223\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#299980\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"58\" y1=\"262\" x2=\"923\" y2=\"262\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1\" /><rect x=\"56\" y=\"269\" width=\"11\" height=\"40\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#299980\"/><text x=\"82\" y=\"295\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">due_date</text><text x=\"288\" y=\"295\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"770\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">null</text><text x=\"588\" y=\"295\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"730\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">nullable</text><path d=\"M854 286 L862 294 L874 277\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#299980\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"58\" y1=\"316\" x2=\"923\" y2=\"316\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1\" /><rect x=\"56\" y=\"323\" width=\"11\" height=\"40\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#db9566\"/><text x=\"82\" y=\"349\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">total</text><text x=\"288\" y=\"349\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"770\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#db9566\">&quot;18.50&quot;</text><text x=\"588\" y=\"349\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"730\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">wrong type</text><path d=\"M855 332 L871 348 M871 332 L855 348\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#db9566\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"58\" y1=\"370\" x2=\"923\" y2=\"370\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1\" /><text x=\"55\" y=\"410\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"680\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">This illustrates checks on stored JSON. It does not call a model or prove its accuracy.</text></svg></div><div class=\"sout-code\"><div class=\"sout-code-head\">Python · Standard library · 15 runnable lines · illustrative JSON only</div><pre style=\"background:#1e1e1e;color:#eff8ff;white-space:pre;overflow-x:auto\"><code style=\"display:block;background:transparent!important;color:#eff8ff!important;border:0!important;padding:0!important;font:inherit;white-space:pre\">import json\nsource = {'order_id':'A-240', 'total':18.5, 'due_date':None}\nsample = '{&quot;order_id&quot;:&quot;A-240&quot;,&quot;total&quot;:18.5,&quot;due_date&quot;:null}'\ndef validate(raw):\n    obj = json.loads(raw)\n    if set(obj) != set(source): raise ValueError('keys')\n    if type(obj['order_id']) is not str: raise ValueError('id type')\n    if type(obj['total']) not in (int,float): raise ValueError('total type')\n    if obj['due_date'] is not None and type(obj['due_date']) is not str: raise ValueError('date type')\n    if obj != source: raise ValueError('source mismatch')\n    return obj\nprint('Validated:', validate(sample)['order_id'])\ntry: validate('{&quot;order_id&quot;:&quot;A-240&quot;,&quot;total&quot;:&quot;18.5&quot;,&quot;due_date&quot;:null}')\nexcept ValueError: print('Wrong numeric type rejected')\nprint('Unknown date:', validate(sample)['due_date'] is None)</code></pre></div><p class=\"sout-note\">The code is fully local and does not call an LLM API.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "How should applications handle refusals, incomplete responses and unsupported schema features when relying on constrained Structured Output generation?",
      "tag": "Advanced · Edge cases and recovery",
      "options": [
        "Treat every model response as complete schema-valid data after requesting strict output. Retry without inspecting completion status, because incomplete responses cannot occur when a schema is supplied.",
        "Parse a refusal as an empty but valid object and continue downstream processing. Silently substituting missing fields is preferable to reporting a safety refusal or asking for review.",
        "Use any JSON Schema keyword and let the model ignore unsupported constraints silently. A schema error is best handled by making the validator accept more fields rather than revising the request.",
        "Check response status and refusals before parsing, recognize truncation or schema errors, and recover according to policy. Never silently convert incomplete or refused responses into trusted records."
      ],
      "answer": "d",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Even when a provider supports constrained structured generation, there can be refusals, incomplete responses or unsupported schema requests. Detect these conditions before parsing or using the data. A receipt extractor that stops mid-response should not store an invented total, and a refusal should not be disguised as a successful empty invoice. Handle retryable failures with limits, correct unsupported schemas and escalate when necessary. Strict formatting is helpful but does not remove application error handling.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"sout-figure\"><span class=\"sout-kicker\">QUESTION 06 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"sout-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 430\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"so-rev6t so-rev6d\"><title id=\"so-rev6t\">Structured generation can have four distinct outcomes</title><desc id=\"so-rev6d\">A fan-out state diagram shows complete response, refusal, truncated output and unsupported schema error, each linked to a different safe next action.</desc><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1000\" height=\"430\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"40\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">06 · STRUCTURED OUTPUT</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"79\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"24\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">Structured generation can have four distinct outcomes</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"120\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">INSPECT COMPLETION STATUS BEFORE PARSING JSON</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"169\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"860\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">MODEL RESPONSE</text><line x1=\"226\" y1=\"161\" x2=\"307\" y2=\"161\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"3\" /><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"161\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#299980\"/><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"178\" x2=\"154\" y2=\"209\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" /><circle cx=\"154\" cy=\"220\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#299980\"/><text x=\"154\" y=\"225\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"860\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\">✓</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"273\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">COMPLETE</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"305\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"720\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">Parse + validate</text><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"178\" x2=\"387\" y2=\"209\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" /><circle cx=\"387\" cy=\"220\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#db9566\"/><text x=\"387\" y=\"225\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"860\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\">!</text><text x=\"297\" y=\"273\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#db9566\">REFUSAL</text><text x=\"297\" y=\"305\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"720\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">Honor refusal</text><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"178\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"209\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" /><circle cx=\"620\" cy=\"220\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#7a80af\"/><text x=\"620\" y=\"225\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"860\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\">!</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"273\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#7a80af\">TRUNCATED</text><text x=\"530\" y=\"305\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"720\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">Retry within limits</text><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"178\" x2=\"853\" y2=\"209\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" /><circle cx=\"853\" cy=\"220\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#448eaf\"/><text x=\"853\" y=\"225\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"860\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\">!</text><text x=\"763\" y=\"273\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#448eaf\">UNSUPPORTED</text><text x=\"763\" y=\"305\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"720\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">Fix requested schema</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"381\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#db9566\">Do not pass a partial invoice to accounting as though it were valid.</text><text x=\"55\" y=\"414\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"685\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">Refusal and truncation are response states, not empty successful objects.</text></svg></div><p class=\"sout-note\">Provider-supported schema subsets and completion states must be handled explicitly.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "How should production Structured Output systems manage schema changes, untrusted input and downstream consumers while monitoring both format reliability and factual accuracy?",
      "tag": "Advanced · Versioning and safety",
      "options": [
        "Version schemas and validators together, test old and new consumers, and keep untrusted text separate from instructions. Track schema compliance and source-checked accuracy with privacy-conscious logs.",
        "Add new required fields directly to every production response without consumer tests, since a JSON object remains parseable. Field compatibility is independent of downstream application behavior.",
        "Let documents being extracted choose the schema and override validator rules. If they contain a field list, treating it as authoritative prevents conflicts with changing task instructions.",
        "Monitor the percentage of parseable JSON only, and keep full sensitive prompts indefinitely for troubleshooting. Schema versioning and source-level quality reviews are unnecessary when parse success is high."
      ],
      "answer": "a",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Structured-output applications are data pipelines, so contract changes affect downstream consumers. Version the schema, tests and parsers together; test backward compatibility and evaluate missing or extra fields. Separate trusted extraction rules from untrusted documents and avoid storing unnecessary sensitive content. For an accounting service, adding `currency` may break a consumer that expects only `order_id` and `total`. Monitor both how often responses meet the schema and whether extracted facts match source records.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"sout-figure\"><span class=\"sout-kicker\">QUESTION 07 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"sout-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 430\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"so-rev7t so-rev7d\"><title id=\"so-rev7t\">Adding currency changes the data contract</title><desc id=\"so-rev7d\">Side-by-side object-key lists show version one with order_id and total, and version two adding currency; a downstream consumer expecting exact keys needs regression testing.</desc><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1000\" height=\"430\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"40\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">07 · STRUCTURED OUTPUT</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"79\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"850\" font-size=\"24\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">Adding currency changes the data contract</text><text x=\"55\" y=\"120\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"840\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">CONTRACT EVOLUTION · A NEW REQUIRED FIELD</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"164\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"860\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#448eaf\">VERSION 1</text><text x=\"513\" y=\"164\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"860\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#299980\">VERSION 2</text><circle cx=\"78\" cy=\"196\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#448eaf\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"202\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">order_id</text><circle cx=\"539\" cy=\"196\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#299980\"/><text x=\"560\" y=\"202\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">order_id</text><circle cx=\"78\" cy=\"248\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#448eaf\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"254\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">total</text><circle cx=\"539\" cy=\"248\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#299980\"/><text x=\"560\" y=\"254\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2c5268\">total</text><circle cx=\"539\" cy=\"300\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#db9566\"/><text x=\"560\" y=\"306\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"840\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#db9566\">currency  ← NEW</text><line x1=\"364\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"364\" y2=\"328\" stroke=\"#d9e8ec\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 6\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"357\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"790\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#db9566\">Consumer expecting exactly two keys may reject version 2.</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"414\" font-family=\"system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif\" font-weight=\"665\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#668290\">Version schema + validator + consumer tests; monitor factual as well as structural quality.</text></svg></div><p class=\"sout-note\">Schema success, factual correctness and security are different quality dimensions.</p></section>"
    }
  ],
